{"name":"Floral Bouquet","hex":"#bacb7c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"floral","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, pertaining to, or connected with flowers.","Portraying flowers, especially in a stylized way."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A design involving flowers","A perfume redolent of flowers"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/floral"},{"term":"bouquet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An arrangement or bunch of cut flowers; a nosegay.","A decoratively arranged bunch of something."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bouquet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Flower bouquet","blocks":[{"text":"A flower bouquet is a collection of flowers in a creative arrangement. Flower bouquets can be arranged for the decor of homes or public buildings or may be handheld. Several popular shapes and styles classify handheld bouquets, including nosegay, crescent, and cascading bouquets. Flower bouquets are often given for special occasions such as birthdays, anniversaries or funerals. They are also used extensively in weddings and at the Olympic medal ceremonies. Bouquets arranged in vases or planters for home decor can be placed in traditional or modern styles. According to the culture, symbolism may be attached to the types of flowers used."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flower_bouquet","wikidata":"Q1187930"},{"title":"Flower","blocks":[{"text":"Flowers, also known as blossoms and blooms, are the reproductive structures of flowering plants. Typically, they are structured in four circular levels around the end of a stalk. These include: sepals, which are modified leaves that support the flower; petals, often designed to attract pollinators; male stamens, where pollen is presented; and female gynoecia, where pollen is received and its movement is facilitated to the egg. When flowers are arranged in a group, they are known collectively as an inflorescence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg/330px-Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flower","wikidata":"Q506"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Onam_Flower_Arrangement.jpg/500px-Onam_Flower_Arrangement.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Onam_Flower_Arrangement.jpg/500px-Onam_Flower_Arrangement.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fresh flowers are arranged in front of houses to celebrate Onam, a major celebration in \nKerala, India.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOnam_Flower_Arrangement.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Ikebana_-_Yoshiko_Nakamura_01B.jpg/500px-Ikebana_-_Yoshiko_Nakamura_01B.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Ikebana_-_Yoshiko_Nakamura_01B.jpg/1280px-Ikebana_-_Yoshiko_Nakamura_01B.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Ikebana_-_Yoshiko_Nakamura_01B.jpg/500px-Ikebana_-_Yoshiko_Nakamura_01B.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Japanese ikebana flower bouquet in a vase","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIkebana_-_Yoshiko_Nakamura_01B.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Beach_Wedding_Bouquet.jpg/500px-Beach_Wedding_Bouquet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Beach_Wedding_Bouquet.jpg/1280px-Beach_Wedding_Bouquet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbna